# DOC-beta: BETA.oot owner-gated exit criteria

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **Paper ID** | `DOC-beta` |
| **Subject document(s)** | `ooda/bootstrap/BETA.oot` |
| **Status** | `draft` |
| **Series** | Documentation system (`DOC-*`) |

## 1. Why this document exists

BETA.oot defines necessary gates for an honest beta tag and states that only the owner may cut the tag. Prevents agents/CI from declaring beta when purity or surface is incomplete.

## 2. Problem statement

Alpha projects often self-label beta when CI is green. openOODA requires constitutional separation: gates ≠ release authority.

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- Release readiness checklists (commercial).
- SRE metrics inform freeze; humans own policy. https://sre.google/sre-book/embracing-risk/
- OSS maintainer authority models.

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

B0–B5 necessary for eligibility; owner sufficient for tagging; agents may report gates green, must not claim beta.

## 5. Limits and failure modes

Gates can be gamed if residuals soft-pass; BETA.oot can lag product.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

Not beta. Document active; cited by README/site.

## 8. Open questions

1. Public proof pack location for B0–B5?
2. Link each B-gate to ROADMAP rows?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Site/README never say beta without owner tag.
- [ ] Agents refuse beta claims.

## 10. References

1. ooda/bootstrap/BETA.oot
2. https://sre.google/sre-book/embracing-risk/

